@page "/"

<PageTitle>GraphQL Practice</PageTitle>

<h1>GraphQL Practice</h1>

<p class="lead">
    A small blog API served with <strong>Hot Chocolate 16</strong> over <strong>PostgreSQL 18</strong>,
    consumed here by a Blazor WebAssembly app using <strong>Strawberry Shake</strong>.
</p>

<div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="card mb-3">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">Explore the client</h5>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="posts">Posts</a> — cursor pagination, filtering and sorting</li>
                    <li><a href="authors">Authors</a> — a generated query component</li>
                    <li><a href="posts/new">New post</a> — a mutation with typed errors</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="card mb-3">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">Explore the server</h5>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="http://localhost:5100/graphql" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nitro IDE</a> — the GraphQL playground</li>
                    <li><a href="http://localhost:5100/graphql/schema" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Schema SDL</a> — the generated schema</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="mb-0 text-muted"><small>Open a post and add a comment to see the WebSocket subscription in action.</small></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<p class="text-muted mt-3">
    See the repository <code>README.md</code> and <code>docs/graphql-tour.md</code> for a guided tour.
</p>
